<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n99768" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνδῐκ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>act as one's advocate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				579
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.2.51
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					937e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				32.12
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς σοι τόδε
			συνδικήσει</span> Zeus <i>will be</i> thy <i>advocate</i>
			herein, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				158
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be one of the public advocates</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύνδικος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ φυλέται οἱ ᾑρημένοι μοι συνδικεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.150
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				20.153
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῷ δήμῳ</span> Lex ap.<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.47
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ βασιλικῷ
			συνδεδικηκώς</span>, = Lat. <i>advocatus
			fisci</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				78.13
			</span></i>.</div>
